      "claim": "FIXED",
      "final_text": "The bug is fixed. Blocked horizontal velocity was only zeroed when the player was on the ground, so an airborne sprint-jump into a wall kept its pointless `vz` and the simulator drifted from the game.\n\n**Change:** in `sim/src/mcsim/physics.py`, `move()` now zeroes `vx` / `vz` whenever that axis was blocked, dropping the `p.on_ground` condition. Vertical handling is unchanged.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Oracle diff on a wall scenario (sprint forward into `wall_v1`, jump at tick 30) diverged at tick 30 on `vz` by 0.0535. After the change it matches with zero delta on all fields.\n- `run_regressions`: 25 scenarios pass, 0 failing, unit tests pass.\n- Saved the reproducing scenario as `wall_airborne_sprint_jump_zeroes_blocked_vz`; it now matches.\n\nI used the Read tool instead of Bash for the source files because one shell command was denied. I did not run `python sim/run.py test` directly, but the lab's regression run includes the unit tests and they passed.\n\nSTATUS: FIXED",
